Z||000000||SN1PERVII||02-07-2000||02:34 PM||||     Hi all. Well It is that time of the year again. I am freezing on by bike and bored to tears in my Izuzu pickup. I have have found 3 fieros in my area for sale.<BR>An 86 SE 87GT ant a 88 coupe. <P>The 88 is is a little rough but seem like a good intirior th front bumper has those circle shaped cracks that makes me think the car has been banged round some it also needs two tires. 5-speed 74500miles $2400 asking price. <P>the other two i have not seen. GT is 2700 SE is 2000.<P>I would like to get the V-6 but I have heard that the maintnance is a pain. I am pretty handy and i work at auto zone so i get a discount on anything in stock so part are not that big of a problem unless we just dont sell it.  (seen it hapen on some pretty basic stuff).<P>How often does the clutch go out on average.<BR>The guys I work with tell some pretty bad horror stories. (only one of them admits to actually working on one. changing the plugs on a six. didnt sound like fun.) <P>Any input would be well come.<P>By the way anybody here ever heard of a town called Gueydan in south LA? any <BR>||||reg||3
Z||000001||wkayl||02-07-2000||04:26 PM||||Changing plugs on a v6 is no problem as long as you remember steps 1 and 2<BR>Step 1: empty trunk<BR>Step 2: stand in trunk<BR>In this position reaching back plugs (firewall side) from the left is a breeze.  I used to work at a Ford dealer in the 70's and it is much easier than a Maverick with a 302.||||reg||1
